; C++ prints an amount through stream_out_mpq (src/amount.cc:208-245),
; which rounds to nearest with ties to even at every stage, so an exact
; decimal tie is decided by the value's binary expansion, not by half
; away from zero.  At precision 1 the postings print A 0.25 as 0.2,
; B 0.35 as 0.3, C 0.45 as 0.5, D 0.15 as 0.2, F 0.55 as 0.6, G 0.65
; as 0.7 and H 0.75 as 0.8 in the rows below, and E's 0.05 rounds to
; 0.0, its row suppressed.  An
; oracle rounding half away from zero instead prints A as 0.3 and B as
; 0.4, and gives the 0.05 tie a 0.1 row where C++ prints none.  The
; semantic bisimulation (test/semantic/check_all.py) replays this
; journal, so such an oracle fails here.

2015/01/01 ties
    A   (0.5 * 0.5 FOO)
    B   (0.5 * 0.7 FOO)
    C   (0.5 * 0.9 FOO)
    D   (0.5 * 0.3 FOO)
    E   (0.5 * 0.1 FOO)
    F   (0.5 * 1.1 FOO)
    G   (0.5 * 1.3 FOO)
    H   (0.5 * 1.5 FOO)
    Z

test bal
             0.2 FOO  A
             0.3 FOO  B
             0.5 FOO  C
             0.2 FOO  D
             0.6 FOO  F
             0.7 FOO  G
             0.8 FOO  H
            -3.2 FOO  Z
